# THE RUST EMITTER'S PROGRAM PASS: a whole program written as one Rust module. It stamps the program (decision 011),
# reads it into the tables compile/rust-emit.tree takes, runs the analyses, asks for each statement, and assembles the
# module from what the emitter recorded (compile/rust-assemble.tree).
#
# Ported from compile/rust.ts `emitRust` and `emitRustPass` (self-hosting, item term-self-host-001-0065), which stays a
# thin face. What the face held by node identity is keyed here by the node's `place-row`: every answer an analysis
# gives about a node (a proven step, a loop's guard, an unsigned division, an ASCII text, an owned inner list, and per
# task the last reads, the slot takes, the slice keys and the cursor reads) is a table of rows, and the emitter's tests
# are closures over those tables. A node the emitter makes for itself stands at no place (row 0) and has no fact, as it
# had none in the face's `WeakMap`s. The places the face numbered by object (compile/place.ts `numberedWalk`,
# ir/facts/interval.ts `identities`) are each their own row here, since a stamped program shares no node.
#
# The program twice when that buys something: a first pass records every clone it writes, and a recursive form whose
# values no pass ever clones has its children held in a `Box` instead of an `Rc` in a second pass (item 0029). Each
# pass reads the stamped program as it was handed: the face's first pass renamed the module's `host` data trees in
# place, so its second pass wrote none of their structs. The `host` data trees are named here on a copy.
#
# The wake chain reads the roll's entries as roll values (decision 040).

load @term/base/list
  find list
  find get

load @term/base/maybe
  find maybe

load @term/base/text
  find starts-with
  find char-at

load @term/base/text/unicode
  find to-runes
  find from-runes

load @term/base/float
  find to-number

load ../parser/diagnostic
  find span

load ./node
  find type
  find expression
  find statement
  find field-value
  find function-param
  find form-field
  find form-variant
  find native-kind
  find expression-type

load ./node-children
  find node-handle
  find node-children
  find block-handles

load ./node-rebuild
  find place-row-of-expression
  find place-row-of-statement

load ./place-stamp
  find stamp-places
  find same-place
  find same-statement-place

load ./place-walk
